y tab.\n\n\n**Implementing Process Modal**\n\nI'm now ensuring the progress modal correctly appears. If a process is running, navigating to the new match screen automatically displays the `#progress-modal`. I've also checked the `#screen-settings` and confirmed the dedicated \"Logs\" section for terminal outputs is included.\n\nI'm revisiting the PDF extraction. The current `parse_items_from_response` in `pdf_reader.py` seems overly rigid and table-dependent. The user is clear that \"the files are different, the formats are different... don't use fixed code.\" I'm now looking at leveraging Gemini API to extract data directly from the unstructured text when table parsing fails, since they provided an API key.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python -c \\\"lines=open('d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/src/extract/pdf_reader.py', encoding='utf-8').readlines(); print(''.join(lines[85:140]))\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"500","toolAction":"\"Check parse_items_from_response\"","toolSummary":"\"Check pdf extraction\""}}]}
